The openLISEM model 
======================
openLISEM is a spatial flood, runoff and erosion model openLISEM. Thank you
for downloading. openLISEM simulates the spatial dynamics of surface runoff and 
erosion for small plots of several m2 to catchments of >1000 km2. 

openLISEM uses the freeware GIS PCRaster (http://pcraster.geo.uu.nl) for database creation and 
analysis of the results. 

openLISEM is developed in Mingw64 for QT, using Qwt, GDAL, OMP, PCRaster and the code from the FUllSWOF project: https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.4125

INSTALL: Download and install the installation package from GitHub: https://github.com/vjetten/openlisem/releases/tag/lisem_bin
This package install also the LISEM dbase generator, and NutShell, an interface for PCRaster

The PCRaster must be installed using (mini)conda (not strictly necessary for openLISEM itself, but for all dbase management):
download and install miniforge, a port of miniconda: https://conda-forge.org/download/
open a conda cmd window and do the following:

	conda create --name lisem python
	conda activate lisem
	conda install -c conda-forge pcraster owslib scipy gdal numpy

(answer ‘y’ to all questions, this will take some time)


